    "prompt": "Function `OptionList.render_line` in src/textual/widgets/_option_list.py. The statements below were written about this exact version of the function.\n\nFunction source (docstring removed):\n```python\ndef render_line(self, y: int) -> Strip:\n        self._populate()\n        assert self._lines is not None\n\n        _scroll_x, scroll_y = self.scroll_offset\n        line_number = scroll_y + y\n\n        try:\n            option_index, y_offset = self._lines[line_number]\n        except IndexError:\n            return Strip([])\n\n        renderable = (\n            Rule(style=self.get_component_rich_style(\"option-list--separator\"))\n            if option_index == -1\n            else self._options[option_index]\n        )\n\n        mouse_over = self._mouse_hovering_over == option_index\n\n        component_class: str | None = None\n\n        if option_index == -1:\n            component_class = \"option-list--separator\"\n        else:\n            try:\n                option = self._options[option_index]\n            except IndexError:\n                pass\n            else:\n                if option.disabled:\n                    component_class = \"option-list--option-disabled\"\n                elif self.highlighted == option_index:\n                    component_class = \"option-list--option-highlighted\"\n                elif mouse_over:\n                    component_class = \"option-list--option-hover\"\n\n        style = (\n            self.get_component_rich_style(component_class)\n            if component_class\n            else self.rich_style\n        )\n\n        strips = self._render_option_content(\n            option_index,\n            renderable,\n            style,\n            self.scrollable_content_region.width - self._left_gutter_width(),\n        )\n        try:\n            strip = strips[y_offset]\n        except IndexError:\n            return Strip([])\n        return strip\n```\n\nFacts extracted from this version by a parser (tree-sitter):\nsignature: render_line(self, y) -> Strip\ncalls: Rule, Strip, self._left_gutter_width, self._populate, self._render_option_content, self.get_component_rich_style\nreturn statements: return Strip([]) | return Strip([]) | return strip\nraise statements: (none)\ncontrol flow: if=4 loops=0 try=3 with=0 returns=3 yields=0 awaits=0\n\n\nStatements:\nS1. `render_line` calculates the absolute line number based on the current scroll offset and the provided `y` value.\nS2. `render_line` ensures that the internal `_lines` attribute is populated by calling `_populate()`.\nS3. The primary side effect of `render_line` is rendering the specified line of the option list to the screen or output buffer.\nS4. If accessing a strip from the result of `_render_option_content` fails due to an `IndexError`, `render_line` again returns an empty `Strip`.\nS5. `render_line` attempts to retrieve the option index and y-offset for the calculated line number from the `_lines` list.\nS6. `render_line` is a function that takes one parameter `y`, which represents the vertical position of the line to be rendered within the visible area of the widget.\nS7. `render_line` retrieves the style for the component class determined and calls `_render_option_content` to generate the content strips for the option.\nS8. If retrieving the option index and y-offset fails due to an `IndexError`, indicating that the line is out of bounds, `render_line` returns an empty `Strip`.\nS9. `render_line` determines whether to render a separator or an actual option based on the retrieved index.\nS10. `render_line` handles errors gracefully by catching exceptions and returning empty results when necessary.\nS11. `render_line` relies on several helper methods, including `_populate()`, `_left_gutter_width()`, and `_render_option_content()`.\nS12. For options, `render_line` checks if they are disabled, highlighted, or hovered over by the mouse to apply appropriate styling.\n\nFor each statement decide: